# /execute's TDD classification markers. Step 3 creates one, Step 6 deletes it —
# they never outlive a commit. One was tracked into this repo by a `git add -A`
# during a dogfooding run and sat at HEAD until a /pre-merge review found it.
# Scoped to the two markers rather than all of `.claude/`, so committing real
# settings or hooks here stays possible.
.claude/.tdd-active
.claude/.tdd-skipped

# The post-review edit lock's two flags. /pre-merge Phase 4 writes the first
# beside the review-currency stamp and /closeout removes it at merge;
# /fix-findings writes the second when it loads and removes it when it reports.
# Same transience as the markers above, and a committed copy of either would
# hold the lock shut or open across every future branch in this repo.
.claude/.review-stamped
.claude/.fix-findings-active
